---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ClientLogos from '../components/ClientLogos.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import ContactButtons from '../components/ContactButtons.astro';

---

<BaseLayout
  title="Fractional marketing for B2B tech companies — Kjell Vandevyvere"
  description="Fractional marketing for B2B tech companies. One person owns strategy and execution: website, positioning, CRM setup and whatever gets the engine running."
>
  <Nav currentPath="/fractional-marketing" />

  <main>

    <!-- ─── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pt-24 pb-24">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h1 class="font-display font-600 text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-[3.25rem] wonk leading-[1.05] text-text-main mb-6">
          <span class="text-coral">Fractional marketing</span> for B2B tech companies.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary font-body leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-xl">
          One person owns strategy and execution, whether you're looking for a new website, better positioning, CRM setup or other projects to get your marketing engine up and running.
        </p>
        <ContactButtons label="Want to talk it through?" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <ClientLogos />

    <!-- ─── THE ENGAGEMENT ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">

      <!-- Recognition first: the reader finds their own week before the offer -->
      <div class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="font-display font-600 text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-text-main leading-snug">
          Do you recognise one of these situations?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl border border-divider shadow-soft p-8 sm:p-10 mb-16">
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          {[
            'Your first marketing hire or fractional GTM just left',
            'Your only marketer is a junior doing their best without anyone to steer them',
            'You\'ve been doing the marketing yourself and it\'s the thing that slips every week',
            'You closed a round and you\'re ready to accelerate GTM',
            'You tried the obvious stuff: a LinkedIn post, a landing page... but nothing moved the needle',
            'The first customers came through your network but you\'re struggling to scale beyond that',
          ].map((item) => (
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-base font-body text-text-main">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-coral mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
              {item}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Then the offer -->
      <div class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="font-display font-600 text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-text-main leading-snug">
          Let's build and improve your marketing foundation from end to end.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-secondary font-body leading-relaxed">
          Your current GTM has a clear problem: nobody owns marketing at a senior level. So the work happens in pieces, and the pieces don't line up. A prospect reads your website, then a LinkedIn post, then your sales deck, and gets three slightly different explanations of what you do. Every new piece gets argued out from scratch because there's no agreed version to write from, and nobody can take the work over without you checking every line.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs font-body font-600 uppercase tracking-wider text-text-secondary mb-6">What gets built</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5 mb-6">
        {[
          { title: 'Positioning and messaging', body: 'ICP, value proposition, and the story your buyer needs before they engage.' },
          { title: 'A website that converts', body: 'Copy and structure built around the positioning, not a redesign exercise.' },
          { title: 'A content motion you can sustain', body: 'The channel that matches your buyer, set up or rebuilt, and running before I leave.' },
          { title: 'Tooling and specialists', body: 'CRM, analytics and automation for your stage, plus who to hire next.' },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl border border-divider shadow-soft p-7 flex flex-col">
            <p class="font-display font-600 text-lg text-text-main leading-snug mb-2">{item.title}</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-body text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        <div class="rounded-3xl border p-7 sm:p-8" style="background: rgba(138, 155, 118, 0.08); border-color: rgba(138, 155, 118, 0.35);">
          <p class="text-xs font-body font-600 uppercase tracking-wider text-sage-deep mb-3">Built for</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-body text-text-main leading-relaxed">
            B2B tech: fintech, deeptech, HRtech, SaaS and infra. The product is live, even if revenue or customers are still early. And it's technical enough that the marketing falls apart when whoever writes it doesn't understand what's being sold.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-3xl border p-7 sm:p-8" style="background: rgba(215, 98, 98, 0.07); border-color: rgba(215, 98, 98, 0.3);">
          <p class="text-xs font-body font-600 uppercase tracking-wider text-coral mb-3">Not for</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-body text-text-main leading-relaxed">
            Companies that already have a marketing lead, because this role is the owner rather than an extra pair of hands. B2C, e-commerce and agencies, where the buying decision works differently. And anything pre-product, where there is nothing to position yet.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-6 text-sm font-body text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-text-main font-600">Scope decides the engagement.</strong> Some companies need a positioning sprint and a website. Others want the full foundation plus ongoing execution. We work that out before anything starts.
      </p>

    </section>

    <!-- ─── THE GTM DASHBOARD ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-24">
      <div class="mb-14">
        <h2 class="font-display font-600 text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-text-main leading-snug">
          The GTM dashboard keeps it all saying the same thing.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-secondary font-body leading-relaxed">
          Marketing drifts when the thinking behind it lives in someone's head. So every engagement runs through a dashboard I built for this, where each brand gets its own structured vault instead of a folder of documents nobody opens twice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-6">
        {[
          { step: 'The layers', body: 'ICP, market and alternatives, messaging, products, voice and brand each live as their own file. Customer transcripts feed the ICP, the ICP feeds positioning, and positioning feeds messaging, so nothing downstream gets invented.' },
          { step: 'The output', body: 'Website copy, LinkedIn posts, the sales deck and email sequences all derive from those files. They tell the same story because they trace back to the same source, not because someone remembered to check.' },
          { step: 'What it changes', body: 'The next piece stops being argued out from scratch, and someone else can pick the work up without you reading every line. On-brand becomes a checkable property rather than a matter of taste.' },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl border border-divider shadow-soft p-7">
            <p class="text-xs font-body font-600 uppercase tracking-wider text-coral mb-3">{item.step}</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-body text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm font-body text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        It started as a chat agent for ICP and positioning, and became a proper app once the pieces needed to connect. More on how it works, and the rest of the AI systems behind this, in <a href="/blog/how-i-use-ai-for-b2b-marketing" class="text-coral font-600 hover:underline">how I use AI for B2B marketing</a>. The messaging it produces follows the structure in <a href="/blog/how-to-write-a-messaging-guide" class="text-coral font-600 hover:underline">how to write a messaging guide</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── HOW IT WORKS ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-24">
      <div class="mb-14 max-w-2xl">
        <h2 class="font-display font-600 text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-text-main leading-snug">
          Why not a strategy consultant or an agency?
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-text-secondary font-body leading-relaxed">
          The usual options split the job in two. You hire someone to decide what should happen, then someone else to make it happen, and the handover between them is where most of the value leaks out.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-6">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 border border-divider shadow-soft">
          <p class="text-xs font-body font-600 uppercase tracking-wider text-text-secondary mb-5">
            Strategy consultants
          </p>
          <p class="font-display font-500 text-text-main text-lg leading-snug mb-3">
            Deliver decks instead of results.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary font-body leading-relaxed">
            Expensive, slow, and then the deck gets handed to a team who then has to figure out what to do with it. The translation from strategy to shipped thing is on you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 border border-divider shadow-soft">
          <p class="text-xs font-body font-600 uppercase tracking-wider text-text-secondary mb-5">
            Freelance operators and agencies
          </p>
          <p class="font-display font-500 text-text-main text-lg leading-snug mb-3">
            Run the channel you ask for, whether or not it fits.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary font-body leading-relaxed">
            Execute tactics without strategic context. Content ships, emails ship, ads ship. Nobody checks whether the positioning underneath holds up, so the signals don't compound.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="rounded-3xl border p-8 sm:p-10" style="background: rgba(215, 98, 98, 0.07); border-color: rgba(215, 98, 98, 0.3);">
          <p class="text-xs font-body font-600 uppercase tracking-wider text-coral mb-5">
            Working with me
          </p>
          <p class="font-display font-500 text-text-main text-lg leading-snug mb-3">
            One person. Strategy and execution. No handoff.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary font-body leading-relaxed">
            Product marketing depth where generalists fall short. Starts with how your buyer moves from problem-aware to decision-ready. Stays hands-on through delivery: the positioning, the website, the sales deck, the content. AI-native workflow that compounds output week over week.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- ─── FAQ ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-24">
      <div class="mb-14 max-w-2xl">
        <h2 class="font-display font-600 text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-text-main leading-snug">
          Common questions
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        {[
          {
            q: 'How long does an engagement last?',
            a: 'Scope decides the length. A positioning sprint is shorter than a full foundation build. Some clients keep me on for ongoing execution after the foundation is in place. We agree on scope first, then map that to a timeline.',
          },
          {
            q: 'What does it cost?',
            a: 'Pricing depends on scope. We go through what needs building first, then you get a clear proposal before anything starts.',
          },
          {
            q: 'Do you work with non-tech companies?',
            a: 'I focus on B2B tech. The frameworks transfer to other categories, but the depth I bring is specific to technical products and technical buyers.',
          },
        ].map((item) => (
          <details class="group bg-white rounded-2xl border border-divider shadow-soft overflow-hidden">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-5 cursor-pointer list-none">
              <span class="font-display font-500 text-text-main text-base">{item.q}</span>
              <span class="text-coral font-display font-600 text-xl group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform flex-shrink-0">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-6 pb-5 -mt-1">
              <p class="text-sm font-body text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">{item.a}</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <ContactCTA />

  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
